      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah it\u0027s more than a little awkward to make opaque though because it\u0027s both an input \u0026 and output (given to `getMetadata`/`setMetadata` but received in the dump callback). So both sides need to be able to conjure an instance of this up. That means any new additions would end up being gated by the interface version, which we could also do by just slapping a 2 or 3 or whatever on the end of a new struct with new sets of get/setMetadatas \u0026 dump callbacks.\n\nEither way it\u0027s going to be clunky if this actually changes, but there\u0027s a _lot_ of flexibility here in a {string, int} key so I think we\u0027re OK.",
