      "writtenOn": "2022-11-03T01:02:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think using the same struct w/ additional methods can make it easier to update code in place. HIDL suggested a whole new struct, and we dropped that whole philosophy with AIDL.\n\nFor instance, if you add \"isSecure\" or some other random small feature, you don\u0027t want to have everyone to have to s/V5/V6/g.",
      "parentUuid": "a4ef74fa_86b3de4e",
      "revId": "899af2180547aa01852f918a9d961adad690d6aa",
